# Globs here are deliberately wide. An uncovered artifact is one `git add .`
# away from becoming tracked content that has to be scrubbed back out again.

# Rust build trees.
target/
**/*.rs.bk

# Bench and bring-up output. Every run of the bench binary against real hardware
# produces transcripts, register dumps and bus traces; none of it is source.
*.log
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
bench-out/
captures/
traces/

# Live bench configuration and the state file the read-only self-test registry
# writes beside it. Both name a specific unit and a specific serial device, so
# they are configured per machine and never tracked.
reachy-bench.toml
reachy-bench.state.toml
*.local.toml
.local/

# Measured geometry and calibration output. Per-unit fitted numbers belong to a
# unit, not to the repo.
calibration/
*.csv

# Except the trace fixtures: a handful of recorded runs kept as test data, so
# the measurements the guards are sized against are replayed by the suite
# instead of remembered. The wide rules above still cover every trace a bench
# session writes. Two lines because a file cannot be re-included out of an
# excluded directory: `traces/` above has to be taken back first.
!crates/reachy-bench/fixtures/traces/
!crates/reachy-bench/fixtures/traces/*.csv

# Personal Claude Code settings (settings.json is shared)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Local secret-scanner rule overrides. Never content in this repo.
.gitleaks.local.toml

# Private per-repo agent context (CLAUDE.md is shared)
CLAUDE.local.md

# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
